    "body": "## Motivation\n\nWith `--enable-linear-replayssm-spec`, KDA models allocate and budget the decode ring's `d`/`k` buffers on every Mamba slot, but spec-verify only reads its fold window (raw v, raw k, the gate, and beta). On GLM-5.3-Flash NVFP4 at TP2 with 512 Mamba slots, `d` and `k` take 2.13 GB each per GPU.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Remove the `d`/`k` rings from the KDA pool under `--enable-linear-replayssm-spec`.\n(note that while `forward_decode` routes on `d`, it doesn't run with this flag, so behavior is unchanged)\n- Remove the KDA `d`/`k` terms from `replayssm_ring_bytes_per_req`, so the sizer gives that memory to the KV pool.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nGLM-5.3-Flash NVFP4 on 2xB200 (TP2/EP2) with a DFlash2 draft, 512 Mamba slots, and ring length 16:\n\n| | main | this PR |\n|---|---|---|\n| `d` / `k` per GPU | 2.13 GB each | 0 |\n| KV cache tokens | 647,680 | 1,024,256 |\n| GSM8K | 0.925 | 0.930 |\n| Accept length | 5.07 | 5.07 |\n\n`test_kda_fold` now expects 2,176 bytes per layer and fails on main. A new case checks that a KDA spec pool allocates exactly the accounted ring bytes. The ring accounting, Mamba allocation, KDA dispatcher, and n-gram verify unit tests pass on CPU (38), and `test_mamba_unittest.py` passes on 1xH200.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nThe compute path is unchanged.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39553064764](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39553064764)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39553064776](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39553064776)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39553064703](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39553064703)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->\n\n\n\n\n\n",
